      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #86): complex residue's tolerant per-
      ⍝ component floor of the quotient decided (correctly) that the
      ⍝ quotient was ⎕CT-close to a Gaussian integer, but then still
      ⍝ returned b - a×floor_quot verbatim -- floating-point
      ⍝ cancellation noise on the order of ⎕CT×|b| from that
      ⍝ subtraction (not caught by comparing the noise itself against 0
      ⍝ or against a) leaked into the result instead of being
      ⍝ recognised as "the true residue is exactly 0".
      ⍝
      0J1E¯11|1
0

      3|2.9999999999999J3
0

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(q)): FloatCell::bif_residue_ff()'s
      ⍝ helper nc_p_modulo_q() deliberately gives up (returns 0)
      ⍝ whenever |B÷A| exceeds 4.5E15, since its own floor()/multiply
      ⍝ steps lose precision beyond that magnitude for a genuinely
      ⍝ fractional quotient -- but that guard has no bearing when B
      ⍝ (here 1E17, a float literal) is itself an EXACT integer: it
      ⍝ must then agree exactly with the same residue computed from the
      ⍝ equal integer literal, which takes IntCell's own, always-exact
      ⍝ path and was never affected by this guard.
      ⍝
      7|1E17
5

      7|100000000000000000
5

      (7|1E17) ≡ 7|100000000000000000
1

      ⍝ control: a genuinely fractional B is unaffected by this fix and
      ⍝ still uses the ordinary (tolerant) float residue path
      ⍝
      7|1E15+0.5
6.5


